1
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:12,920
Brighten up the peace
and step back to see it.

2
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:28,580
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling out.

3
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:32,640
I walked on, looking back.

4
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:35,280
Led by the hand by Ga-chan,

5
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:42,420
the strange feeling I had back then.

6
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:47,700
So, on the arcade guide tiles,

7
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,480
I tried walking only on the black parts.

8
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:59,660
Everyone was a child once,

9
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,780
but everyone has forgotten.

10
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:09,080
Pompous-faced politicians and
aunties with blue eyeshadow too,

11
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:14,660
go on, turn around that corner.

12
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:19,900
You can meet everyone, everyone.

13
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:27,800
There it is, Kame-ari! Surely there's a turtle
(Kame-ari)!

14
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:33,080
Everyone, come on over to our town!

15
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:34,560
Thank you.

16
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:39,640
Fight for the bonus battle!

17
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:48,780
Wow, this is...

18
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:53,860
In first-generation CI Hot Gang circles,
this is the ultimate treasure!

19
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:58,140
And it's mint condition with the box. I never
expected something like this to be in this shop.

20
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:01,540
A toy shop I know is closing down.

21
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:04,620
So I'm taking over their merchandise.

22
00:02:04,620 --> 00:02:06,100
This was among it.

23
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:07,820
How much?

24
00:02:07,820 --> 00:02:09,660
So you don't intend to sell it?

25
00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:11,820
I was thinking of displaying it in the shop.

26
00:02:11,820 --> 00:02:13,300
Please, sell it to me!

27
00:02:15,340 --> 00:02:17,100
If you insist on it,

28
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:19,080
how about this much?

29
00:02:19,860 --> 00:02:20,980
That's too expensive!

30
00:02:20,980 --> 00:02:24,020
At least it should be
around this much, right?

31
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:25,940
Hey, how about this?

32
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:27,800
No, a bit more.

33
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:29,140
Hey, how about this?

34
00:02:29,140 --> 00:02:31,660
I won't give you a single
penny off beyond this.

35
00:02:32,780 --> 00:02:35,560
Alright, I win.

36
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:36,480
Thanks for your business.

37
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:39,160
What's this hand for?

38
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:41,400
What do you mean what? It's payment!

39
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:43,280
Unfortunately, I don't have any cash on me.

40
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:44,620
I'll pay you later.

41
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:48,580
We're a cash-only business.

42
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:50,340
He says he'll pay later.

43
00:02:50,980 --> 00:02:52,040
Can you trust him?

44
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:53,140
No way.

45
00:02:53,980 --> 00:02:56,280
You didn't have to be so blunt about it.

46
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:57,640
Honestly, Ryo-san,

47
00:02:57,640 --> 00:03:00,760
how many tabs do you think you've
stiffed us on over the years?

48
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:02,600
Did that really happen?

49
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:03,980
Loads of times.

50
00:03:04,420 --> 00:03:05,580
And it's not just us.

51
00:03:05,580 --> 00:03:08,480
The liquor store, the greengrocer, the candy shop,
the electronics shop, the ramen shop.

52
00:03:09,420 --> 00:03:11,080
All of us here in the shopping street

53
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:12,800
have suffered so much. Do you have
any idea what we've been through?

54
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,940
I still can't sell this, sorry.

55
00:03:16,940 --> 00:03:18,400
Please, just sell it to me.

56
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:20,100
I'll pay you later, I promise.

57
00:03:20,980 --> 00:03:22,800
Anyone without money, get out.

58
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:24,460
My bonus is coming up soon.

59
00:03:24,460 --> 00:03:25,880
I'll pay with that.

60
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:29,840
I think there's someone in the third
block who likes this kind of thing.

61
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:32,120
Please, I'll really pay.

62
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:33,380
This time, for sure.

63
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:35,440
You say that every year, you know.

64
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:38,240
This year, I really, truly mean it.

65
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:40,120
Look me in the eyes.

66
00:03:41,740 --> 00:03:42,580
They're murky.

67
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:45,700
Please, Bramoya!

68
00:03:45,700 --> 00:03:48,860
I promise, I'll definitely pay.

69
00:03:48,860 --> 00:03:51,720
Even so, a verbal promise doesn't count.

70
00:03:51,720 --> 00:03:54,180
I'll write up a contract
or whatever you want.

71
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:58,720
In that case, you'll sign this.

72
00:03:58,720 --> 00:03:59,580
What's this?

73
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:01,620
It's sort of like a contract.

74
00:04:01,620 --> 00:04:03,780
Now, sign right here.

75
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:04,800
Fine.

76
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:06,660
Don't forget your seal, too.

77
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:09,740
Yes! I finally got it!

78
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:13,700
Thanks for your business!

79
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:21,680
Old man, please!

80
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:23,860
Ryo-san, you're in a good mood!

81
00:04:24,260 --> 00:04:26,480
I got my hands on a rare figure.

82
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:29,100
I was thinking of raising a toast tonight.

83
00:04:29,860 --> 00:04:31,240
Well, that's great.

84
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:34,220
Let's see, then, the total comes to...

85
00:04:34,220 --> 00:04:35,220
See ya.

86
00:04:35,220 --> 00:04:37,860
Hey, hey, Ryo-san! You haven't paid yet!

87
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:39,320
Put it on the tab, my tab!

88
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:40,780
I'll pay with my bonus.

89
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:43,500
I've been fooled by those words every year.

90
00:04:43,980 --> 00:04:45,820
If you really want to put it on the tab...

91
00:04:46,440 --> 00:04:48,260
Then have him sign this.

92
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:51,520
Signing is a piece of cake.

93
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:52,920
My darling

94
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:56,360
Whoa.

95
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:58,520
W-what is all this?

96
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:04,000
Once I got the first-generation CI Castle,
I started wanting things to decorate it with.

97
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:04,720
I just couldn't help it.

98
00:05:04,720 --> 00:05:05,800
Unbelievable.

99
00:05:06,220 --> 00:05:08,060
Doesn't that cost quite a bit?

100
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:09,280
Yeah, well.

101
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:11,100
Where did you get the money for all this?

102
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:12,600
Before your bonus, too?

103
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:16,260
Put it all on my tab.
I'll pay you back with my bonus.

104
00:05:16,260 --> 00:05:16,800
Yo!

105
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:17,220
Hey.

106
00:05:17,220 --> 00:05:22,180
Ryo-chan, every year you say that, buy all sorts of stuff,
and then just let it slide, don't you?

107
00:05:22,180 --> 00:05:24,760
You're causing trouble for
people on the shopping street.

108
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:26,960
This year, you'd better pay properly.

109
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:29,480
Yeah, yeah. What a nagging woman.

110
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:31,480
That's why no one will
ever want to marry you.

111
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:32,700
Did you say something?

112
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:34,220
Nothing.

113
00:05:34,980 --> 00:05:37,140
Thanks as always! It's Surugaya!

114
00:05:37,140 --> 00:05:39,820
You're here. Just set it down over there.

115
00:05:40,660 --> 00:05:41,020
Yes.

116
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:43,540
That'll be 750 yen.

117
00:05:43,540 --> 00:05:44,940
Just put it on my tab.

118
00:05:44,940 --> 00:05:46,080
Ryo-chan.

119
00:05:46,640 --> 00:05:48,220
I don't have any cash on me right now.

120
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:49,420
What else can I do?

121
00:05:49,420 --> 00:05:52,100
Then you shouldn't have ordered
delivery in the first place.

122
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:54,540
What's done is done,
so there's no helping it.

123
00:05:54,980 --> 00:05:55,300
Ugh.

124
00:05:55,300 --> 00:05:56,720
You're always making excuses.

125
00:05:57,400 --> 00:05:59,220
Shall I cover it for you?

126
00:06:00,200 --> 00:06:00,840
It's fine.

127
00:06:00,840 --> 00:06:01,940
When it's on credit,

128
00:06:02,540 --> 00:06:05,340
I've been told to have
you sign this document.

129
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:07,340
Sign it.

130
00:06:07,340 --> 00:06:08,340
Fine, I guess.

131
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:14,460
Yes, I've received it. Thank you very much.

132
00:06:17,940 --> 00:06:19,120
What was that just now?

133
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:24,320
Yeah, lately whenever I shop on the shopping street,
they always make me sign something.

134
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:26,020
You didn't check it?

135
00:06:26,020 --> 00:06:30,080
It's like a pledge, right?
It says to pay properly with the bonus.

136
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:36,620
Now that you mention it, a copy of some
document came in earlier, didn't it?

137
00:06:36,620 --> 00:06:37,900
Where is it?

138
00:06:38,340 --> 00:06:40,340
I tore it up and threw it away somewhere.

139
00:06:42,780 --> 00:06:43,500
Like this?

140
00:06:44,480 --> 00:06:45,520
Yeah, that's right.

141
00:06:45,520 --> 00:06:47,540
That one there, next to the...

142
00:06:47,540 --> 00:06:48,900
Really.

143
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:52,380
W-what is this?

144
00:06:52,380 --> 00:06:52,780
Well,

145
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:53,880
what's wrong?

146
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:57,420
The document Senpai
signed isn't just a pledge.

147
00:06:57,420 --> 00:07:00,020
It's an agreement for a large automatic
withdrawal from your bank account.

148
00:07:00,020 --> 00:07:02,500
A large amount? A bank account? What's that?

149
00:07:03,140 --> 00:07:06,540
In other words, the money will be automatically taken
from Ryo-chan's bank account

150
00:07:06,540 --> 00:07:09,360
to pay for the goods.
It's a contract to withdraw the big sum.

151
00:07:09,360 --> 00:07:10,100
I see.

152
00:07:11,020 --> 00:07:12,100
So that's the trick.

153
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:13,840
Is that so?

154
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:16,000
Can you really do that?

155
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:17,440
You can.

156
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:22,720
Isn't that how it works for electricity,
gas, water, and even credit card purchases?

157
00:07:23,780 --> 00:07:25,100
Now that you mention it,

158
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:27,060
Well, that's good then, Ryo-chan.

159
00:07:27,060 --> 00:07:29,500
No need to go out of your
way to pay a large sum,

160
00:07:30,020 --> 00:07:33,040
though your bank account
will be empty in no time.

161
00:07:34,260 --> 00:07:34,620
No way...

162
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:35,620
No way!

163
00:07:36,580 --> 00:07:39,460
Now then, the 29th

164
00:07:39,460 --> 00:07:44,120
Ryotsu Kankichi Bonus Battle
strategy meeting is now open.

165
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:47,380
That's what I'd like to say, but...

166
00:07:50,120 --> 00:07:51,220
Congratulations!

167
00:07:52,460 --> 00:07:57,040
This year's bonus battle is officially ours.

168
00:07:57,500 --> 00:08:00,460
Today is a free-for-all.
Enjoy yourselves to the fullest.

169
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:04,460
Well, I never imagined
there was a method like this.

170
00:08:04,460 --> 00:08:08,200
Ryo-san's salary has been paid by bank transfer for two years now,
after all.

171
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:10,560
I wish I'd realized this sooner.

172
00:08:10,960 --> 00:08:13,780
Honestly, I don't really like
this sort of way of doing things.

173
00:08:14,140 --> 00:08:17,060
Money moving around behind your back without you knowing,
you know.

174
00:08:17,060 --> 00:08:21,760
Well, well, well. Thanks to this, my missus
says she'll be coming back, so there's that.

175
00:08:21,760 --> 00:08:23,460
Hey, you model-kit peddler!

176
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:29,340
You two were in cahoots, you swindlers!

177
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:32,520
Making me sign this crap!

178
00:08:33,180 --> 00:08:35,640
I didn't force you to sign.

179
00:08:36,140 --> 00:08:38,540
Ryo-san, you signed it of your own accord,
didn't you?

180
00:08:38,540 --> 00:08:40,260
You said it was a pledge.

181
00:08:40,940 --> 00:08:43,140
I said it was a contract.

182
00:08:43,140 --> 00:08:45,700
Isn't it that you misheard, Ryo-san?

183
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:48,620
Y-you bastard, you calculated all of this?

184
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:52,260
Or did you think you could ignore a pledge,

185
00:08:52,660 --> 00:08:53,980
or something?

186
00:08:53,980 --> 00:08:56,760
No, that's not it.

187
00:08:56,760 --> 00:08:59,920
I'm just saying I don't like this method.

188
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:07,860
I was going to pay each of you back with my own hands,
as a token of my gratitude for all this time.

189
00:09:07,860 --> 00:09:09,280
And yet -

190
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:11,760
We don't need your gratitude at all.

191
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:14,000
All we want is the money back.

192
00:09:15,340 --> 00:09:23,240
Besides, weren't you the type of man, Kankichi Ryotsu,
who suddenly hates to pay once the cash is right in front of him?

193
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:27,560
T-that's...

194
00:09:27,560 --> 00:09:27,960
That's...

195
00:09:28,540 --> 00:09:30,280
Damn it! You'll pay for this!

196
00:09:31,560 --> 00:09:32,400
Yes!

197
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,340
It's not such a bad deal at all!

198
00:09:36,860 --> 00:09:39,522
If that's how it is,
I'll have my bonus paid in cash,

199
00:09:39,572 --> 00:09:41,640
not transferred to the bank.
I have no choice, but

200
00:09:41,780 --> 00:09:44,480
how do I convince the
people at headquarters...

201
00:09:45,300 --> 00:09:46,160
Just as I thought...

202
00:09:46,160 --> 00:09:49,020
Honestly,
don't just toss newspapers around like that!

203
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:52,760
That's it!

204
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:59,420
200 grams of pork, carrots, and onions.

205
00:10:00,180 --> 00:10:00,980
And also,

206
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:03,600
Chief, I have something to discuss with you.

207
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:07,440
It's nothing.

208
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:10,360
The supermarket on the second
block of Naka-chō has a special sale.

209
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:12,840
So I just need to buy it there, right?

210
00:10:14,180 --> 00:10:15,220
Got it.

211
00:10:18,220 --> 00:10:20,860
A chief of the Katsushika police box,
of all people,

212
00:10:20,860 --> 00:10:22,320
running errands for dinner?

213
00:10:22,760 --> 00:10:23,600
How pathetic.

214
00:10:24,180 --> 00:10:25,820
I've always been like this,
so leave me alone.

215
00:10:25,820 --> 00:10:28,180
Have you really always been like this?

216
00:10:28,580 --> 00:10:28,980
What?

217
00:10:29,640 --> 00:10:31,780
Actually,
it's not just the chief's household,

218
00:10:32,260 --> 00:10:35,240
but across all of Japan,
fathers' authority has been declining.

219
00:10:35,680 --> 00:10:36,920
The cause is entirely

220
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:40,220
the switch to salaries
being paid by bank transfer.

221
00:10:40,220 --> 00:10:41,820
No way!

222
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:44,340
Can you really say that for certain?

223
00:10:44,780 --> 00:10:46,060
Think back, please,

224
00:10:46,060 --> 00:10:50,520
to the day when fathers came home
carrying their thick bonus envelopes.

225
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:53,920
A thick bonus envelope!

226
00:10:55,860 --> 00:10:56,480
I'm home!

227
00:10:57,180 --> 00:10:58,380
Welcome home!

228
00:10:58,940 --> 00:11:00,380
Alright, it's bonus time!

229
00:11:00,920 --> 00:11:02,240
Wow, it's bonus time!

230
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:05,260
Dear, thank you for
your hard work as always.

231
00:11:12,220 --> 00:11:15,420
Shall we all go shopping this Sunday?

232
00:11:15,420 --> 00:11:16,340
Yay!

233
00:11:16,340 --> 00:11:17,480
Thank you, dear.

234
00:11:18,340 --> 00:11:19,780
Tonight we're having sukiyaki!

235
00:11:20,520 --> 00:11:21,280
Yes, dear.

236
00:11:22,020 --> 00:11:23,240
Wow, I love it!

237
00:11:26,480 --> 00:11:27,460
I-indeed.

238
00:11:27,820 --> 00:11:29,984
Back then, as a father and as a husband,

239
00:11:30,034 --> 00:11:32,420
he was far more respected than he is now.

240
00:11:32,640 --> 00:11:33,240
Right?

241
00:11:33,820 --> 00:11:36,300
When the father brought his salary home,

242
00:11:36,420 --> 00:11:40,700
everyone in the family could feel who
it was that made their lives possible.

243
00:11:41,060 --> 00:11:43,360
In today's era,
where salaries are paid by bank transfer,

244
00:11:43,540 --> 00:11:47,220
there's no way for respect
for fathers to arise.

245
00:11:47,220 --> 00:11:50,180
We should switch back to
cash payment right away.

246
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:54,580
But doing that would be a lot of hassle,

247
00:11:54,580 --> 00:11:57,760
and I'm not asking you to do
that for monthly salaries too.

248
00:11:57,760 --> 00:12:02,080
Shouldn't at least the
bonus be paid in cash?

249
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:04,160
But

250
00:12:04,660 --> 00:12:09,760
Chief, have you ever been thanked
just because a bonus came in recently?

251
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:12,160
Now that you mention it, last year...

252
00:12:14,460 --> 00:12:15,320
I'm home.

253
00:12:17,560 --> 00:12:19,100
Hey, what's all this?

254
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:21,320
With the bonus I bought it.

255
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:22,520
You bought it?

256
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:24,360
Without even consulting me?

257
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:26,580
And had it moved all the way to my room?

258
00:12:30,020 --> 00:12:31,800
without a word of consultation,

259
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:33,500
buying a PC just for himself,

260
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:36,000
and not even a single thank-you!

261
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,660
It's my bonus, you know!

262
00:12:38,460 --> 00:12:40,300
Chief, now is the time we must do it!

263
00:12:40,300 --> 00:12:42,820
To restore fathers' authority,

264
00:12:42,820 --> 00:12:45,680
bonuses should go back
to being paid in cash!

265
00:12:47,220 --> 00:12:49,280
Let's set this example!

266
00:12:51,420 --> 00:12:53,460
Understood! Tondagomes!

267
00:12:53,720 --> 00:12:57,480
Once more, to restore fathers' authority,
let's make a bold decision!

268
00:12:57,740 --> 00:13:00,100
This year's bonus will be paid in cash!

269
00:13:00,440 --> 00:13:02,780
Yosh! As expected of a man!

270
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:13,200
This is terrible! We got the graphics card!

271
00:13:14,520 --> 00:13:24,580
Kikuchi, today's finally the day the mass-production loan comes back.
It's turned into something outrageous. Look at this.

272
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:30,520
Yeah, if that bonus is paid in cash...

273
00:13:31,900 --> 00:13:35,700
The boss got carried away
and blabbed everywhere.

274
00:13:36,260 --> 00:13:39,900
Ryo-san, I'll let you know when
the cash transport van arrives.

275
00:13:40,360 --> 00:13:42,840
If you keep hanging around there,
you'll just be in the way.

276
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:44,980
What's it matter where I am?

277
00:13:44,980 --> 00:13:48,340
I just want to get my bonus
before anyone else does.

278
00:13:54,860 --> 00:13:55,900
Those guys

279
00:13:56,340 --> 00:13:57,320
It's a seasonal tradition, isn't it.

280
00:13:57,320 --> 00:13:57,500
Hey.

281
00:13:58,440 --> 00:14:00,340
The bonus still hasn't been paid out

282
00:14:00,740 --> 00:14:03,580
Looks like the cash transport
truck is running late.

283
00:14:03,580 --> 00:14:05,500
Alright, standby for payment!

284
00:14:06,260 --> 00:14:09,100
That's why I was against
that plan from the start.

285
00:14:09,940 --> 00:14:12,320
There's no point going now, is there?

286
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:15,800
Plamoya-san, what kind of plan
have you prepared this time?

287
00:14:16,620 --> 00:14:16,940
Mm.

288
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:21,560
Operation Sky Eye,
using a satellite navigation system.

289
00:14:22,020 --> 00:14:25,920
And Operation Peeping Eye,
using surveillance cameras around town.

290
00:14:27,320 --> 00:14:31,460
The debt-collecting weapon I developed
for use against Officer Ryotsu,

291
00:14:31,460 --> 00:14:32,780
Shocking X!

292
00:14:33,540 --> 00:14:35,940
Isn't it just the same
plans that failed before?

293
00:14:35,940 --> 00:14:39,260
We didn't have time to prepare,
so it can't be helped!

294
00:14:41,560 --> 00:14:44,560
Besides, I'll power up Shocking X.

295
00:14:44,560 --> 00:14:46,640
It's Shocking X Marks!

296
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:50,440
Something's wrong!

297
00:14:51,080 --> 00:14:52,620
Hey, that guy there...

298
00:14:53,640 --> 00:14:56,660
That's one of our young guys who
was guarding the cash transport truck!

299
00:14:57,320 --> 00:14:57,440
What?

300
00:14:58,160 --> 00:14:59,560
Hey, pull yourself together!

301
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:02,680
What happened?
What became of the cash transport truck?

302
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:07,160
It was stolen by a pair of robbers.

303
00:15:07,160 --> 00:15:07,740
What?

304
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:14,820
Damn you, how dare you take my bonus -

305
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:17,640
Catch Ryo-san!

306
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:24,280
Here! What are you doing? Get down!

307
00:15:25,220 --> 00:15:27,900
We can't let Ryo-san act freely.

308
00:15:27,900 --> 00:15:30,400
If we fail to get the
cash transport truck back,

309
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:32,980
you won't get any money either, you know.

310
00:15:33,700 --> 00:15:36,600
But if Ryo-san finds it first,

311
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:40,760
he could take only his
own bonus and run off.

312
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:42,240
R-really?

313
00:15:42,240 --> 00:15:45,700
I would never do that!
I will pay, I really do intend to pay.

314
00:15:46,100 --> 00:15:48,920
But every year it's just been
"intending to," hasn't it?

315
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:51,060
Damn it, then...

316
00:15:51,060 --> 00:15:52,400
With this...

317
00:15:55,560 --> 00:15:57,220
Emergency broadcast. Emergency broadcast.

318
00:15:57,720 --> 00:16:00,180
A cash transport truck was attacked
within Katsushika Station's jurisdiction,

319
00:16:00,180 --> 00:16:02,600
and the bonuses for the entire
Katsushika Station were stolen.

320
00:16:03,440 --> 00:16:07,060
I repeat, the stolen items were the
bonuses of the entire Katsushika Station.

321
00:16:07,680 --> 00:16:09,180
The culprits are a pair of men.

322
00:16:09,540 --> 00:16:11,040
They are fleeing in a white van.

323
00:16:11,640 --> 00:16:14,260
All personnel,
give your all and apprehend them.

324
00:16:21,180 --> 00:16:22,040
Bonuses.

325
00:16:27,180 --> 00:16:28,820
What do we do, Plamoya?

326
00:16:29,620 --> 00:16:33,080
If Ryo-san gets to it first,
we're in big trouble.

327
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:36,280
We'll get the cash transport
truck back ourselves.

328
00:16:45,620 --> 00:16:47,160
That's a lot of patrol cars.

329
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:49,820
Our own bonuses are on the line, after all.

330
00:16:51,620 --> 00:16:53,620
The man who first reported it

331
00:16:54,060 --> 00:16:56,080
Didn't he run all the way to the station?

332
00:16:59,680 --> 00:17:02,540
Yeah, apparently the culprits took his radio,
his cell phone,

333
00:17:02,540 --> 00:17:04,420
and even his coin purse, they say.

334
00:17:04,420 --> 00:17:07,020
It must have been to buy time, I bet.

335
00:17:07,020 --> 00:17:10,540
But I don't think it
would buy them much time.

336
00:17:10,540 --> 00:17:15,060
What were the culprits even
doing in that short time?

337
00:17:16,900 --> 00:17:17,700
What's wrong?

338
00:17:18,060 --> 00:17:22,320
Well, just now a blue van with
terrible paint streaks was driving by.

339
00:17:22,320 --> 00:17:26,820
Never mind that! The culprits' van is white!

340
00:17:27,640 --> 00:17:34,240
Sorry, sorry. I'm just a stickler by nature,
so sloppy work always bugs me.

341
00:17:34,740 --> 00:17:39,080
Got it, that's the culprits' van!

342
00:17:46,740 --> 00:17:48,540
What do you mean, Plamoya?

343
00:17:48,960 --> 00:17:50,700
They repainted the car's color.

344
00:17:51,360 --> 00:17:54,480
It may seem impossible to
repaint it in such a short time,

345
00:17:55,100 --> 00:17:58,040
but they only need to fool
the police temporarily.

346
00:17:58,760 --> 00:18:00,340
They pull into a place out of sight

347
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:03,780
and cover the windshield with newspaper,
then spray paint.

348
00:18:04,580 --> 00:18:07,540
If you look closely,
you'd notice something unnatural right away,

349
00:18:07,540 --> 00:18:10,000
but the police are looking for a white van.

350
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:11,960
There's a chance they'll overlook it.

351
00:18:12,620 --> 00:18:14,240
I see. Well done.

352
00:18:14,240 --> 00:18:15,740
You're a real man.

353
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:20,180
This year we're finally going to win,
Ryo-san.

354
00:18:26,160 --> 00:18:28,760
Police! Open the back of the truck.

355
00:18:28,760 --> 00:18:29,740
Y-yes.

356
00:18:33,360 --> 00:18:35,400
Senpai, this isn't them.

357
00:18:36,220 --> 00:18:37,320
Alright, you can go.

358
00:18:48,080 --> 00:18:49,520
What's going on with those guys?

359
00:18:50,280 --> 00:18:52,400
Don't tell me they found
the cash transport truck.

360
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:55,140
Nakagawa, go after them! Hurry!

361
00:18:55,140 --> 00:18:55,480
Yes, sir!

362
00:18:55,940 --> 00:18:59,480
It looks like the blue van headed
from Nishi-Kabeari toward Horikiri.

363
00:18:59,480 --> 00:19:00,200
Understood.

364
00:19:00,740 --> 00:19:03,020
Found it! That's the blue van from before!

365
00:19:03,500 --> 00:19:04,500
Good work!

366
00:19:05,840 --> 00:19:08,840
Right, don't let them get away.
We'll catch up right away!

367
00:19:13,780 --> 00:19:15,260
Whatever you do, don't lose them!

368
00:19:18,760 --> 00:19:20,440
Money, in a place like this...

369
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:21,540
Money...

370
00:19:21,540 --> 00:19:22,400
Stop!

371
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:28,400
Where is it, where's the money?

372
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:30,760
I was sure I had a 500-yen coin here.

373
00:19:32,620 --> 00:19:34,900
Damn it, it's just an arcade token!

374
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:37,140
Senpai, what are you doing?

375
00:19:37,140 --> 00:19:39,640
I just did it out of reflex.

376
00:19:40,660 --> 00:19:41,960
This is no time for this.

377
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:43,500
I have to get my bonus back.

378
00:19:46,400 --> 00:19:49,200
Damn, I lost sight of it!

379
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:53,040
Stop that car!

380
00:19:53,040 --> 00:19:58,040
Stop right there!

381
00:19:58,620 --> 00:20:01,160
Found the van!

382
00:20:03,720 --> 00:20:05,000
Halt!

383
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:13,280
Stop!

384
00:20:15,260 --> 00:20:17,620
The time has come for it
to show its true power.

385
00:20:30,320 --> 00:20:31,860
Now they can't escape.

386
00:20:34,660 --> 00:20:36,120
Stay still and don't resist.

387
00:20:36,120 --> 00:20:37,180
Y-yes.

388
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:40,300
Damn it!

389
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:42,340
They should be around here somewhere.

390
00:20:49,840 --> 00:20:51,060
What do we do now?

391
00:20:51,060 --> 00:20:53,580
At this rate,
the culprits are going to get away.

392
00:20:53,580 --> 00:20:56,980
Isn't there some way to contact the police?

393
00:20:56,980 --> 00:20:58,420
Like this, we can't.

394
00:20:58,420 --> 00:21:00,580
You're all so useless.

395
00:21:00,580 --> 00:21:03,240
Don't we have a special method for this?

396
00:21:04,160 --> 00:21:05,400
A special method?

397
00:21:06,360 --> 00:21:07,860
Like this, of course.

398
00:21:09,740 --> 00:21:12,520
There's a stack of cash lying around here!

399
00:21:12,520 --> 00:21:14,760
There's a stack of cash lying there.

400
00:21:15,260 --> 00:21:17,388
There's a stack of cash lying there!

401
00:21:17,438 --> 00:21:19,400
There's a stack of cash lying there!

402
00:21:20,460 --> 00:21:21,940
A stack of cash?!

403
00:21:22,540 --> 00:21:24,400
Over there, Nakagawa! Hurry!

404
00:21:25,140 --> 00:21:27,080
But what about the model shop's car?

405
00:21:27,200 --> 00:21:29,820
Forget the model shop's car,
the cash is right in front of us!

406
00:21:31,180 --> 00:21:32,340
That's dangerous!

407
00:21:32,420 --> 00:21:33,160
Get out of the way!

408
00:21:40,620 --> 00:21:41,000
What?

409
00:21:42,820 --> 00:21:44,280
Where's the cash?!

410
00:21:45,260 --> 00:21:48,580
Hey... Seven, don't tell me that's -

411
00:21:49,940 --> 00:21:55,180
That's the cash transport truck!
That guy's the culprit!

412
00:21:55,700 --> 00:21:59,940
The culprit's inside this one,
and in that one is my bonus -

413
00:22:00,520 --> 00:22:03,400
They're coming! Can't you see this?

414
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:06,160
Give back my bonus!

415
00:22:06,160 --> 00:22:06,680
Me.

416
00:22:14,820 --> 00:22:15,780
Get out of the way, geez!

417
00:22:17,740 --> 00:22:18,560
Aaaaaah!

418
00:22:20,320 --> 00:22:21,800
We did it, senior!

419
00:22:22,260 --> 00:22:24,480
My bonus, my bonus!

420
00:22:24,480 --> 00:22:25,380
Ryo-san

421
00:22:28,800 --> 00:22:30,860
You're going to pay back my debts, right?

422
00:22:31,580 --> 00:22:31,900
That's...

423
00:22:34,280 --> 00:22:35,240
He's going to run off!

424
00:22:35,560 --> 00:22:38,260
Somewhere along the way,
I'll quietly pull out just my bonus.

425
00:22:38,260 --> 00:22:39,520
Oh well!

426
00:22:44,500 --> 00:22:44,960
Thanks.

427
00:22:49,360 --> 00:22:51,300
Bonus improvement!

428
00:22:56,880 --> 00:22:58,280
This year's bonus

429
00:22:58,280 --> 00:23:01,480
You know who you have to thank
for getting it back, right?

430
00:23:01,480 --> 00:23:02,360
That's right.

431
00:23:02,360 --> 00:23:05,120
You should thank the shopkeepers.

432
00:23:05,120 --> 00:23:06,500
I know.

433
00:23:07,140 --> 00:23:09,820
At least this year,
I'll pay you back properly.

434
00:23:13,200 --> 00:23:16,220
Community Section One, Kankichi Ryotsu-san

435
00:23:18,500 --> 00:23:19,960
Alright, good work.

436
00:23:20,960 --> 00:23:22,320
This is awfully thin.

437
00:23:26,880 --> 00:23:28,920
It's 613 yen.

438
00:23:29,900 --> 00:23:32,040
Hey, this has to be some
kind of mistake, right?

439
00:23:32,040 --> 00:23:33,680
No, it's not.

440
00:23:34,180 --> 00:23:35,020
Chief.

441
00:23:36,140 --> 00:23:38,460
This is all I've got for my bonus!

442
00:23:38,460 --> 00:23:39,640
What's going on here?

443
00:23:40,300 --> 00:23:43,740
In your case,
you've broken all sorts of office equipment.

444
00:23:44,240 --> 00:23:46,220
I deducted it from your bonus.

445
00:23:47,680 --> 00:23:48,600
No way!

446
00:23:49,100 --> 00:23:50,680
Didn't make it this year either

447
00:23:50,680 --> 00:23:52,840
I'll definitely get it next year.

448
00:23:52,840 --> 00:23:55,300
Well, after all that hard work...

449
00:23:56,060 --> 00:23:57,680
I don't accept this!

450
00:24:01,200 --> 00:24:05,520
Kicked the alarm clock,
stubbed my pinky toe, ow-ow-ow!

451
00:24:05,520 --> 00:24:13,780
Quickly draw my eyebrows, then
dance-dance-dance all the way to the station!

452
00:24:13,780 --> 00:24:19,520
Packed commuter train,
a quick nap on Dad's back.

453
00:24:20,580 --> 00:24:25,840
Another hard week, and the
unreasonable demands are only natural.

454
00:24:26,980 --> 00:24:33,280
Looking all posh with a baguette in hand,
but it's really a beef bowl with extra soup.

455
00:24:33,280 --> 00:24:40,240
Overtime irritation piling up,
cleared away with ylang-ylang!

456
00:24:43,780 --> 00:24:50,020
Every day's No Problem, after a hot shower.

457
00:24:50,020 --> 00:24:56,600
Every day's No Problem,
energy restored with a sleep pillow.

458
00:24:59,540 --> 00:25:06,200
Every day's No Problem,
I love myself just the way I am.

459
00:25:06,200 --> 00:25:12,920
Every day's No Problem,
hearts flying on a Monday.

460
00:25:20,140 --> 00:25:21,120
This is bad!

461
00:25:21,120 --> 00:25:23,900
Nakagawa and I have switched bodies!

462
00:25:23,900 --> 00:25:24,780
Wait a minute.

463
00:25:24,780 --> 00:25:27,880
That means I'm the heir
to the Nakagawa Group!

464
00:25:27,880 --> 00:25:29,560
Money to spend to my heart's content.

465
00:25:29,560 --> 00:25:31,160
All the delicious food I can eat.

466
00:25:31,160 --> 00:25:33,160
Well, this is simply irresistible!

467
00:25:33,680 --> 00:25:34,320
Different.

468
00:25:34,320 --> 00:25:36,000
Body-jack, what a disaster!

469
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:37,200
Nice to meet you.

470
00:25:38,540 --> 00:25:40,720
Over there is Kamearii.

471
00:25:41,640 --> 00:25:43,700
Surely Kameari!

472
00:25:43,700 --> 00:25:49,100
Everyone, come to our town!

473
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:50,720
Thank you.

